    "created_at": "2017-08-03T18:49:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-08-03T18:49:28Z",
    "body": "AFAIK, the only reason other events have an event-specific dict is because they have extra arguments to the dict.  There's no reason to make a BeforeUnloadEventInit dict that subclasses EventInit and doesn't add anything to it.\r\n\r\nI never speak for Gecko!  I'd be happy to write a Gecko patch, but I'm not the one to decide if it will be accepted.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
